  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is shown to have targets that ultimately lead to the Dual specificity tyrosine-phosphorylation-regulated kinase 1B (DYRK1B) through multiple distinct pathways. The first pathway involves Oblonganoside C acting on Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, which is targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol, and Ent-Gloeosteretriol in turn targets DYRK1B. The second pathway links Oblonganoside C to BRISTOL8, which is targeted by flavopiridol, and flavopiridol also targets DYRK1B. The third pathway connects Oblonganoside C to Macrophage colony-stimulating factor 1 receptor, which is targeted by Ent-Gloeosteretriol, and again leads to DYRK1B. These pathways collectively suggest that Oblonganoside C exerts its effects through multiple intermediate targets that ultimately converge on DYRK1B. The strength of the evidence is consistent across the three paths, with scores ranging from 0.6121 to 0.6484, indicating a moderate level of confidence in the relationship. The mechanisms involve kinase targeting and signaling pathways, but the exact nature of the interactions remains to be fully elucidated."
